# Coding standards (required)

## Comments and docstrings

- **No essay comments.** Do not narrate what the code does, restate the
  function name, or leave multi-paragraph “why we did this” blocks in source.
- Comment only when the *intent* is non-obvious (invariant, quirk, workaround).
  Prefer one short line.
- Do not add module/class/function docstrings that only repeat the signature
  or walk through the implementation. Existing short module headers are fine;
  do not expand them into essays.
- CHANGELOG / PR bodies: short bullets, not prose essays.

## Style

- Match existing code. No drive-by refactors or unrelated file edits.
- Prefer public names for cross-module symbols; `_` only for true module-locals.
